The largest predictions are for these Chinese/Japanese characters; nearby
kana identifies Japanese use, and two familiar compounds get lower values.
Smaller predictions cover connection/continuity words, translations of
'even', and related East Asian forms (including the similar lotus characters
莲/蓮). Byte-split characters are recovered from the decoded prefix.
Everything else is zero: weak background responses are not modeled.
"""
